==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|delicate|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdɛlɪkətli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-delicately.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|del|i|cate|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[delicate]] manner; exquisitely.
#: {{ux|en|The gingerbread was '''delicately''', if imprecisely, captured by the brushstrokes.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1978|title=Pruning and Grafting|author=Oliver E. Allen|page=93|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=iZlzeSBRTe4C
|passage=The intergrown foliage atop a xylosma hedge appears to be '''delicately''' balanced on long wooden fingers.}}
# [[tactfully|Tactfully]].
#: {{ux|en|He approached the main subject '''delicately'''.}}

